==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[pay]]-[[as]]-[[you]]-[[go]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|economics}} A financial policy by which [[capital]] projects are [[finance]]d from current revenue in the operating budget rather than through borrowing.
# {{lb|en|British}} A payment method where [[credit]] is purchased in advance, used in small amounts and [[topped up]] when required. Used especially of [[mobile phones]] and transport ticketing.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 January 2|title=First official Transport for London trains operate to Reading|journal=Rail|page=10|text=From January 2, passengers will be able to use [[contactless]] '''pay-as-you-go''' between London and [[Reading]].}}

